it's late afternoon in mexico city  and rosa silva is out searching for her  daughter victoria lisbeth who went  missing last year  an anonymous phone call has led rosa to  a part of the city that's popular among  sex workers  she believes whomever took her daughter  may have forced her into prostitution  all of this is in hopes of finding my  daughter victoria it would be the  greatest thing that could happen for us  to find her during one of these searches  that we carry out with the help of elena  elena is the founder of an ngo that  seeks to help people like rosa in their  search for missing loved ones  some time ago we received a phone call  it was a woman's voice she said she had  seen rosa's daughter among the girls out  here  elena's organization has started a  campaign called cuartos vasilos or empty  rooms in spanish  their main objective is to raise  visibility over the crisis of missing  persons in mexico by symbolically  renting out the rooms of missing women  the money they raise is used to help  families fund the search for their loved  ones  this room once belonging to rosa's  daughter victoria is just one of tens of  thousands of empty rooms across mexico  though victoria has been missing for  more than a year rosa has kept  everything just the way it was the day  her daughter disappeared  something tells me my daughter is alive  but where is she i wish i could just  turn the corner and see her and hold her  i dream of her constantly in my dreams i  see my daughter smiling i see her coming  home  i have faith that i will find my  daughter all i ask is for god to give me  the strength to continue this struggle  apart from the pain of not knowing where  victoria is or if she's even alive rosa  has all but spent her life savings  trying to find her  and in mexico it's a story that plays  out every day in households all across  the country  more than 22 100 women are currently  listed as missing in mexico and more  than half of them are under the age of  18. the crisis of missing persons in  mexico is so massive that every day an  average of six women go missing most of  them will never be seen or heard from  again  as weeks and months have passed with no  updates on victoria's whereabouts many  have lost faith of ever finding her  alive  rosa however refuses to give up hope  vowing to never give up the search for  her daughter  manuel rapalo al jazeera mexico city
 

